  "notes": "Audit, modified cash basis, FYE 9/30/2022. Same choices as Waco FY2023. Governmental funds: General, Special Revenue (Street, Keno, ARPA sub-columns) and Debt Service; business-type: Sewer and Water enterprise fund. Statement lines from Exhibit D Total Governmental Funds (p5); State receipts 59,561.15 split by the Exhibit G state sources breakdown (p8), its 'Other state sources' 4,526.07 further by the fund schedules (homestead 4,314.46, carline 211.61); Other general receipts 68,451.26 split by fund schedules (General 6,053.43 p10, Special Revenue 62,397.83 p11). Both capital outlay lines are Street column / Exhibit G Public works - street. Transfers 21,984.20 recorded gross from fund columns (Total column prints '-'). Business-type lines from the Statement of Activities (p2-3); roll-forward -76,187.50 + 55,335.88 - 51,613.73 = -72,465.35 (p3); business-type receipts total from Exhibit F total operating receipts (p7), disbursements total from Statement of Activities (p2, includes capital outlay 27,265.00 that Exhibit F shows as nonoperating). Governmental fund balance: 971,117.51 + 291,923.78 - 261,465.37 + 21,984.20 - 21,984.20 = 1,001,575.92. No prior-year cash printed, so beginning_cash null; ending_cash = cash in bank + county treasurer (p4), CDs in ending_investments. Detail from the departmental analyses (Exhibits H-K, p10-13); Exhibit G budgetary comparison (p8-9, all funds combined) not recorded in detail to avoid double counting. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}
